B2 done — verified for real, with two genuine findings along the way.

What's built: envelope.py — pydantic v2 models matching §5's wire schema exactly (Event → EventEnvelope → EventDetails/EncryptionMetadata/RecipientKey), frozen, with to_wire()/from_wire() round-trip serialization and default factories for eventId (UUIDv7) and eventCreated so callers don't have to remember either. signature stays optional here on purpose — B3 is what actually signs.

10 tests, all passing, covering round-trip fidelity, the exact key-set match against §5, UUIDv7 uniqueness/ordering, frozen-model immutability, and required-field validation.

Two things only running it (not writing it) surfaced:

Confirmed empirically — not assumed — that pydantic serializes an aware UTC datetime with a Z suffix (2026-08-24T22:09:17.515177Z), matching §5's documented example format rather than drifting to +00:00.
pydantic's mypy plugin doesn't understand populate_by_name=True — even with the plugin enabled (pydantic.mypy, now in root pyproject.toml), it still expects camelCase aliases in the synthesized __init__. Confirmed by actually turning the plugin on and watching it still fail, not assumed from memory. Handled with one narrowly-scoped type: ignore[call-arg] at the single call site that exercises snake_case construction, with a comment explaining why — not a blanket suppression.
