This confirms watch() uses genuine server-side NATS wildcard filtering (correctly excluded the unrelated orders key) — good, but it also revealed real complexity worth handling deliberately: a None entry marks "caught up to live," and TTL-based expiry (nats-server 2.11+) arrives via a MaxAge marker mapped to a PURGE operation, distinct from explicit DEL but needing the same cache-removal handling. Let me clean up leftover test state, then design registry.py around these confirmed behaviors.

