This is a real, substantial fix — not just documentation. Since it directly touches registry.py and bus_client.py (both already built and tested), I'll implement it now: a new service-identity KV bucket (permanent, no TTL — unlike recipient liveness, an identity's signing key doesn't need to expire), registered once at connect time, and — critically — verification will look up the trusted key from this directory rather than trusting the message's own embedded sourcePublicKey. That's the actual fix; the embedded field alone was the whole problem.

