Renders clean. Design.md is now fully updated for Phase 2 planning.

Phase 2 scoped and documented — nothing built yet, per the "design first, build on continue" rhythm.

Added to Design.md:

Decisions #21 and #22 in §2's ledger — the two things Phase 2 genuinely needed settled before it could be scoped: how the Webhook Listener verifies an inbound request (generic shared-secret header, since no real source is being integrated yet — same placeholder spirit as Decision #14), and the webhook→command mapping (URL path segment → file path, raw body → base64 content).
A new §12, "Phase 2 — Detailed Breakdown", mirroring §11's format exactly: a parameters table (adapter package naming, both payload shapes, path-traversal handling, the HTTP port, the data volume), then three tracks:
Track C — File Storage Adapter (C1–C7): scaffold → settings → schemas → the write-path command handler → the external-creation watch (watchfiles, per Decision #19) → entrypoint → tests. Built and verified standing alone first, since it's the piece the other track needs something to prove against.
Track D — Webhook Listener (D1–D5): scaffold → settings → the HTTP endpoint → entrypoint → tests.
Track E — Integration (E1–E4): docker-compose wiring, Dockerfiles, a manual smoke test (A7's pattern, this time through real HTTP), and an automated end-to-end test (B7's test_end_to_end.py pattern, extended past the library into real adapters).
One real correction caught while scoping, not building: §7.1's original repo layout sketched a generic app/ package name for every adapter — that collides under uv's single shared workspace venv (two adapters can't both own a top-level app module in one site-packages). Fixed the layout to name each package after its adapter, matching jetcore's own convention, and left a note explaining why.
§9's open-questions list updated: item #1 (File Storage Adapter command schema) is now marked partially resolved — the write path is fully specified for Phase 2, list/read/delete remain deferred to Phase 3 as before.
Sequencing is deliberately linear this time (C → D → E) rather than Phase 1's parallel tracks, since there's nothing for the Webhook Listener to prove against until the File Storage Adapter actually works. Ready for "continue on to Step C1" whenever you want to start building.

